/* F hands K to h, whose type demands a function from the trees qin accepts
   (t and f) to the trees qarg accepts.  K returns a t or a f, both of which
   qarg accepts, through one of its two transitions on a each.  An
   abstraction that joins K's two outcomes into one choice node below a
   checks the choice from one of those transitions and rejects it, which
   is a refutation no input causes: the property holds. */
%BEGING
F h -> h K.
K y -> a (case y of t => t | f => f).
%ENDG

%BEGINA
qin t -> .
qin f -> .
qarg a -> q1.
qarg a -> q2.
q1 t -> .
q2 f -> .
qo ok -> .
%ENDA

%BEGINT
F : ((qin -> qarg) -> qo) -> qo.
%ENDT
